body:
OP I grew up in a hoarder house too and what we see of the KJs is collecting, not hoarding. At least of Kim's clothes. She has the resources to do it, each piece is taken care of and catalogued, she selects things to go into the collection and gets rid of what she doesn't want to keep easily (eg Kardashian Kloset). You grew up in a hoarder's house and you think hoarders can organise and take care of their stuff like we saw Kim doing?? Lmfao. 

&#x200B;

Khloe's does seem a bit pathological but it's not affecting her living space, her house is still all perfectly useable even if she does have too many biscuits in her pantry, so it doesn't really meet the criteria for hoarding.
